                <pb facs="0615" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6286: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-29T16:00:00-05:00">October 29, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. Your 39, October 28, 7 p.m. Consul at Dakar reported October 27 that General
                    Weygand had arrived there October 26. Accordingly, there would appear to be no
                    further question of your acting as intermediary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
